[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404613974","pull_request_review_id":3302499449,"id":2404613974,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6PU39W","diff_hunk":"@@ -570,6 +570,7 @@ public:                                              \\\n                                                      \\\n private:\n \n+class ClassDB;","path":"core/object/object.h","commit_id":"5935a32e323bbf5766837cf43c178d4149336717","original_commit_id":"ce89cd61a0bc8a5492bc5fc815c55aa998ec3b56","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'm surprised `object.h` doesn't include ClassDB (anymore?).\r\n\r\nDoesn't that mean that any Object that wants to register properties with `ADD_PROPERTY` now needs to include `ClassDB`, which is far from obvious?\r\n\r\nIf that's the only coupling it does make sense to remove it of course, but then do we need to go one step further and turns `ADD_PROPERTY` and friends into member methods which are implemented in `object.cpp` (including `class_db.h`), so callers don't need to include it?","created_at":"2025-10-05T18:48:00Z","updated_at":"2025-10-05T18:48:00Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111297#discussion_r2404613974","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111297","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404613974"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111297#discussion_r2404613974"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111297"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404613974/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":569,"original_line":573,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404618874","pull_request_review_id":3302502973,"id":2404618874,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6PU5J6","diff_hunk":"@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@\n \n #include <cstdlib>\n \n+class MainLoop;","path":"core/os/os.h","commit_id":"5935a32e323bbf5766837cf43c178d4149336717","original_commit_id":"ce89cd61a0bc8a5492bc5fc815c55aa998ec3b56","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"(Oof, GH failed to send my comment, need to retype it all again...)\r\n\r\nSo this one warrants discussion. It may be worth it, but it's a bit of an anti-pattern IMO to forward-declare a class that it returns by a public method of a class (here `MainLoop *OS::get_main_loop()` and `void OS::set_main_loop(MainLoop *p_main_loop)`.\r\n\r\nIt means that any class that uses this API from `OS` not only needs to include `core/os/os.h`, but also `core/os/main_loop.h`. That's unconventional IMO, and leads to surprises, as it seemed to be the case for you:\r\n\r\n> The latter was inconsequential, but the former revealed several dependency chains for `core/os/main_loop.h`, despite neither it _nor the compilation file_ using `MainLoop` in any way.\r\n\r\nThose compilation files all use MainLoop via `OS::get_singleton()->get_main_loop()`.","created_at":"2025-10-05T18:59:47Z","updated_at":"2025-10-05T18:59:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111297#discussion_r2404618874","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111297","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404618874"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111297#discussion_r2404618874"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111297"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404618874/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":43,"original_line":43,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404619323","pull_request_review_id":3302503392,"id":2404619323,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6PU5Q7","diff_hunk":"@@ -570,6 +570,7 @@ public:                                              \\\n                                                      \\\n private:\n \n+class ClassDB;","path":"core/object/object.h","commit_id":"5935a32e323bbf5766837cf43c178d4149336717","original_commit_id":"ce89cd61a0bc8a5492bc5fc815c55aa998ec3b56","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"That exact confusion is why I'm wanting to migrate the macros to `class_db.h` instead:\r\n- #110939 \r\n\r\nI will note that an explicit `ClassDB` include in compilation files is the paradigm that GDExtension uses, so I don't think it's inherently harmful. But it isn't the most obvious include either, so making them member functions instead could work out","created_at":"2025-10-05T19:01:14Z","updated_at":"2025-10-05T19:02:33Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111297#discussion_r2404619323","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111297","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404619323"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111297#discussion_r2404619323"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111297"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404619323/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":569,"original_line":573,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2404613974,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404625328","pull_request_review_id":3302508797,"id":2404625328,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6PU6uw","diff_hunk":"@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@\n \n #include <cstdlib>\n \n+class MainLoop;","path":"core/os/os.h","commit_id":"5935a32e323bbf5766837cf43c178d4149336717","original_commit_id":"ce89cd61a0bc8a5492bc5fc815c55aa998ec3b56","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Hmm... I'm not sure if I agree with it being an anti-pattern. If this was the *only* thing this class did then maybe, but not every file that calls `OS` is doing so for `MainLoop`.\r\n\r\nThey led to surprises for me because the implicit link is now broken, but that's an inevitability with this type of change. If we're wanting to move more towards including files with intent, then weeding out those that aren't is the price we gotta pay","created_at":"2025-10-05T19:16:59Z","updated_at":"2025-10-05T19:16:59Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111297#discussion_r2404625328","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111297","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404625328"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111297#discussion_r2404625328"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111297"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404625328/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":43,"original_line":43,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2404618874,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404634780","pull_request_review_id":3302515844,"id":2404634780,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6PU9Cc","diff_hunk":"@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@\n \n #include <cstdlib>\n \n+class MainLoop;","path":"core/os/os.h","commit_id":"5935a32e323bbf5766837cf43c178d4149336717","original_commit_id":"ce89cd61a0bc8a5492bc5fc815c55aa998ec3b56","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I agree that it's not optimal. Ideally C++ wouldn't put us in a position where we choose between usability of an interface and compile time, but unfortunately that's just how the language is. Like Repiteo, I don't consider it an anti-pattern, just an inconvenience.\r\n\r\nBesides needing to omit includes in some locations for technical reasons (cyclic dependencies), we have a problem of _extremely_ long include chains in some spots. We _will_, I'm fully convinced, make the trade-off of requiring an additional include in some locations. From my perspective, this is a matter of judging each situation on a case by case basis.\r\n\r\nIn this specific instance, I'd say that it's worth it, because `OS` is a kitchen sink class, where only a handful of users will interface with the `MainLoop` class.","created_at":"2025-10-05T19:40:49Z","updated_at":"2025-10-05T19:45:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111297#discussion_r2404634780","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111297","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404634780"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111297#discussion_r2404634780"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111297"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404634780/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":43,"original_line":43,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2404618874,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404646642","pull_request_review_id":3302524754,"id":2404646642,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6PU_7y","diff_hunk":"@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@\n \n #include <cstdlib>\n \n+class MainLoop;","path":"core/os/os.h","commit_id":"5935a32e323bbf5766837cf43c178d4149336717","original_commit_id":"ce89cd61a0bc8a5492bc5fc815c55aa998ec3b56","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Should we make it a policy to document such incomplete return types with some comment that shows up in IDEs? What syntax gets picked up, `///` comments?","created_at":"2025-10-05T20:11:29Z","updated_at":"2025-10-05T20:11:30Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111297#discussion_r2404646642","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111297","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404646642"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111297#discussion_r2404646642"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111297"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404646642/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":43,"original_line":43,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2404618874,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404651179","pull_request_review_id":3302529011,"id":2404651179,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6PVBCr","diff_hunk":"@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@\n \n #include <cstdlib>\n \n+class MainLoop;","path":"core/os/os.h","commit_id":"5935a32e323bbf5766837cf43c178d4149336717","original_commit_id":"ce89cd61a0bc8a5492bc5fc815c55aa998ec3b56","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"To further illustrate my point, given the platform-related changes in this PR, I fully expect that this will cause a compilation error for third-party platform ports (e.g. consoles, homebrews) when they update. It could also potentially break a first-party platform we don't test on CI, though I think that's only visionOS and its calls to `OS::get_main_loop` are all shared with iOS through `drivers/apple_embedded`.\r\n\r\nBut yeah, I agree that this is worth doing for `OS` in this case. It's indeed a very commonly included class while only a handful of includers need to call `get_main_loop()`, so that's a good rationale for making it an incomplete definition.\r\n\r\nNote that the title of this commit/PR is a bit misleading, as the biggest impact of this PR is the change to `core/os/os.h` which is not in `core/config`.","created_at":"2025-10-05T20:22:38Z","updated_at":"2025-10-05T20:30:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111297#discussion_r2404651179","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111297","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404651179"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111297#discussion_r2404651179"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111297"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404651179/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":43,"original_line":43,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2404618874,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404658623","pull_request_review_id":3302534527,"id":2404658623,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6PVC2_","diff_hunk":"@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@\n \n #include <cstdlib>\n \n+class MainLoop;","path":"core/os/os.h","commit_id":"5935a32e323bbf5766837cf43c178d4149336717","original_commit_id":"ce89cd61a0bc8a5492bc5fc815c55aa998ec3b56","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> Should we make it a policy to document such incomplete return types with some comment that shows up in IDEs? What syntax gets picked up, `///` comments?\r\n\r\nDoxygen-style suggestion and some extra include cleanup in MainLoop:\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/core/os/main_loop.h b/core/os/main_loop.h\r\nindex baa6a528cd..2d5b1e3635 100644\r\n--- a/core/os/main_loop.h\r\n+++ b/core/os/main_loop.h\r\n@@ -30,9 +30,8 @@\r\n \r\n #pragma once\r\n \r\n-#include \"core/input/input_event.h\"\r\n #include \"core/object/gdvirtual.gen.inc\"\r\n-#include \"core/object/ref_counted.h\"\r\n+#include \"core/object/object.h\"\r\n \r\n class MainLoop : public Object {\r\n \tGDCLASS(MainLoop, Object);\r\ndiff --git a/core/os/os.h b/core/os/os.h\r\nindex a002646121..c99860e5dd 100644\r\n--- a/core/os/os.h\r\n+++ b/core/os/os.h\r\n@@ -223,6 +223,7 @@ public:\r\n \r\n \tvoid ensure_user_data_dir();\r\n \r\n+\t/// @note MainLoop is forward-declared in OS and should be included to use this.\r\n \tvirtual MainLoop *get_main_loop() const = 0;\r\n \r\n \tvirtual void yield();\r\n```\r\n(Feel free to word this better.)","created_at":"2025-10-05T20:41:08Z","updated_at":"2025-10-05T20:41:43Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111297#discussion_r2404658623","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111297","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404658623"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111297#discussion_r2404658623"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111297"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404658623/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":43,"original_line":43,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2404618874,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2404690387","pull_request_review_id":3302560728,"id":2404690387,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6PVKnT","diff_hunk":"@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@\n \n #include <cstdlib>\n \n+class MainLoop;","path":"core/os/os.h","commit_id":"5935a32e323bbf5766837cf43c178d4149336717","original_commit_id":"ce89cd61a0bc8a5492bc5fc815c55aa998ec3b56","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.co